+## Parameter values as type parameters
+
+All parameter structs are defined with
+  [`ClimaParams.@params`](https://clima.github.io/ClimaParams.jl/dev/API/#ClimaParams.@params)
+  instead of `@kwdef`.
+By default (the "type" mode of the `CLIMA_PARAMS_MODE` preference), this
+  macro moves the field values into a type parameter, so every parameter struct
+  is a singleton whose values are compile-time constants.
+The compiler folds them into the code that reads them, which removes them from
+  the arguments of GPU kernels and lowers their register usage.
+Parameter structs are constructed, read and dispatched on the same way in both
+  modes, except for `getfield` and `fieldtype`, which return `nothing` and
+  `Nothing` in "type" mode: read a field with `getproperty` (`p.field`), and
+  get its type with `typeof(p.field)`.
+
+Because every set of values is a different type, code that uses a new set of
+  values is compiled again.
+Applications that construct many sets of values, such as calibrations and
+  parameter sweeps, should switch to "bits" mode, in which `@params` is
+  equivalent to `@kwdef` and new values need no recompilation.
+To do this, add the following to the `Project.toml` of the environment that
+  runs them, and restart Julia (the mode is fixed during compilation):
+
+```toml
+[preferences.ClimaParams]
+CLIMA_PARAMS_MODE = "bits"
+```
+
+The documentation of `ClimaParams.@params` describes both modes in more
+  detail, including how to set the preference from a script.
+
 ## Overriding parameter values
 
 Overrides are applied when the `ParamDict` is created, so a single override
